wh40k-tips-dataset-1 = Psyker, remember: the warp is unstable. Cast steadily — the more spells, the higher the backlash chance, and at peak instability a catastrophe seals every psyker for the rest of the round.
wh40k-tips-dataset-2 = A Commissar can execute an ally before the final wave to buff the whole team. Losing one fighter pays off with extra damage and speed for several minutes.
wh40k-tips-dataset-3 = The Chaplain cannot fire guns at all. Your arsenal is the Sacred Dash through enemy lines, bible healing, and projectile reflection.
wh40k-tips-dataset-4 = The Astartes is a superhuman: takes far more punishment than a human, but moves slower in its armor. Standard armor won't fit — only Astartes plate.
wh40k-tips-dataset-5 = An Ork doesn't give up while alive: its body knits wounds even in critical state. Hold on while blood flows — you can still fight.
wh40k-tips-dataset-6 = Battle phases matter. In preparation the fight is locked — build and upgrade. In assault the economy doubles, and in apocalypse it triples.
wh40k-tips-dataset-7 = Don't waste preparation on reinforcements. Pump the upgrade tree at the command node — passive income and machine speed pay off in the assault.
wh40k-tips-dataset-8 = Maxing out the command node's upgrade level roughly doubles passive income — money flows into the treasury much more often.
wh40k-tips-dataset-9 = Influence points fall faster when many fighters stand on them. A trio takes a point three times quicker than a lone wolf.
wh40k-tips-dataset-10 = Officers and squad leaders earn the team triple points per enemy kill. Protect your commanders — they're the heart of the economy.
wh40k-tips-dataset-11 = The tactical map only shows what's near allies. Move as a group and the fog of war recedes ahead of you, revealing enemy positions.
wh40k-tips-dataset-12 = The officer tablet can draw on the map. Mark enemy points and danger directions before the team pushes in.
wh40k-tips-dataset-13 = A psyker levels up by meditating in a bed — experience flows faster. Don't repeat the same spell back-to-back, or backlash builds.
wh40k-tips-dataset-14 = In astral projection the psyker takes half damage, but any attack from them breaks the trance. Protect the psyker while they project.
wh40k-tips-dataset-15 = A Khorne heretic cuts through enemy lines with Bloodstorm Dash — a dash through the crowd that knocks down and maims. The Chosen of Khorne can dash three times in a row.
wh40k-tips-dataset-16 = Stay close to a Tzeentch leader — the aura speeds up ability cooldowns for the whole cult. The closer you are, the more often you cast.
wh40k-tips-dataset-17 = The plasma gun is dangerous to its user: it sometimes overheats and explodes in your hands. Don't squeeze the trigger for no reason.
wh40k-tips-dataset-18 = The melta gun hits hard, but only point-blank. Get up close to armored targets — at range it's useless.
wh40k-tips-dataset-19 = Weapons have mod slots: optics, suppressor, bipod, sling, bayonet. A sniper scope noticeably extends your aiming range.
wh40k-tips-dataset-20 = A bipod zeroes spread and recoil, but only while you're prone. A light machine gun in a trench is death to attackers.
wh40k-tips-dataset-21 = A weapon sling saves you from a shameful drop: on stun, slip, or crit the gun stays in your hands.
wh40k-tips-dataset-22 = Hook the Fulton balloon to enemy corpses — the team earns points for each extracted body. Hauling your own dead is pointless, no reward.
wh40k-tips-dataset-23 = A supply drop is expensive and slow to recharge. Agree with the team who calls the crate and when, so you don't waste the balance.
wh40k-tips-dataset-24 = The Vox backpack is a shop on your back: meds, ammo, mortar shells for war funds. Only works under open sky.
wh40k-tips-dataset-25 = The ore extractor works faster the higher your team level. Roof it over, or the weather will eat it alive.
wh40k-tips-dataset-26 = A gas mask saves you from radiation and spores. A hardsuit protects from ash, acid rain, hail, and sandstorm. Keep protection handy.
wh40k-tips-dataset-27 = Ion storm, black ice, gellar tremor, and machine corrosion hit with NO protection. Build roofs over positions — your only shield.
wh40k-tips-dataset-28 = Machine corrosion devours vehicles and turrets. Pull iron off open positions when this storm rolls in.
wh40k-tips-dataset-29 = Orbital bombardment blankets the map with falling explosions. Don't stand in the open when the sky burns — wait it out in cover.
wh40k-tips-dataset-30 = Black Front doubles income from influence points but disables normal weather. Seize the moment and capture points while it lasts.
wh40k-tips-dataset-31 = In Wave Defence, critical enemies still count as alive. Finish off the downed, or the wave won't end and the next piles on.
wh40k-tips-dataset-32 = Chaos Astartes show up from wave 20 in Wave Defence. Focus fire on them — a bolter in a giant's hands leaves no chance.
wh40k-tips-dataset-33 = In Gun Game your weapon changes with every frag. The goal is to reach level thirty and take the win. Crit = death, so don't rambo.
wh40k-tips-dataset-34 = In Gun Game a death streak without frags lowers your level. Play more carefully — better pick your moment than charge in.
wh40k-tips-dataset-35 = In Murder Mystery, collect seven clues and you become the sheriff with a revolver. Only civilians can collect — not the murderer or current sheriff.
wh40k-tips-dataset-36 = The sheriff's pinpointer in Murder Mystery only points at the revolver when it's lying on the floor. In someone's hands there's no arrow — you can't sniff out the holder.
wh40k-tips-dataset-37 = In Prop Hunt the seeker can fire a pulse that highlights hiders in a radius. Save the charge — the recharge is long.
wh40k-tips-dataset-38 = After a few rounds on one faction you'll get a warning, then a hard lock. Alternate sides so you don't lose your pick.
wh40k-tips-dataset-39 = The "Fireline Initiation" achievement is earned for a kill streak in a round and grants the "Legend" title. Grind combat achievements if you like aggressive play.
wh40k-tips-dataset-40 = The Astartes dash is short, but it knocks the enemy down and stuns them. Break through a melee line to reach the shooters behind.
wh40k-tips-dataset-41 = Don't stand idle on a capture point — if you all die, progress starts to melt. Keep at least one fighter to hold it.
wh40k-tips-dataset-42 = The command node is your faction's heart. If it's destroyed in Wave Defence, the round is lost. Defend it at any cost.
wh40k-tips-dataset-43 = New psyker? Start with the Sanctioning discipline — it lowers spell backlash and speeds up astral projection.
wh40k-tips-dataset-44 = The Biomancy discipline heals allies. A Biomantic Surge in skilled hands replaces a field surgeon.
wh40k-tips-dataset-45 = The psyker's Aegis wall seals a corridor from enemies. Use it to block an advance or cover a retreat.
wh40k-tips-dataset-46 = Warp Step bails you out when you need to reposition fast. But every jump raises instability — don't teleport without reason.
wh40k-tips-dataset-47 = A Nurgle heretic raises corpses as zombies. Finish off fallen allies so the enemy can't turn them against you.
wh40k-tips-dataset-48 = A Slaanesh heretic can swap places with an enemy. Use it to pull an officer out of fire or drag a victim into an ambush.
wh40k-tips-dataset-49 = A Chaos leader can sacrifice a follower for warp and cult experience. Do it only in the assault phase — it won't work in preparation.
wh40k-tips-dataset-50 = A bayonet on a rifle turns it into a spear: a powerful thrust replaces the stock bash. Don't forget melee when the ammo runs dry.
wh40k-tips-dataset-51 = A long barrel speeds up bullets and cuts spread, but slows you down. A short barrel is the opposite: faster run, worse shooting.
wh40k-tips-dataset-52 = A suppressor isn't just quiet — it kills the muzzle flash too. Perfect for ambushes and night maps.
wh40k-tips-dataset-53 = A folding stock collapses for mobility and unfolds for accuracy. Unfold before a fight, fold on the move.
wh40k-tips-dataset-54 = The Krieg lasgun with bayonet is a trench weapon. The thrust pierces armor, and the laser beam burns at range.
wh40k-tips-dataset-55 = The hellgun fires fast and hard, but feeds from a backpack generator. Without the pack it's a useless hunk of iron — check your gear.
wh40k-tips-dataset-56 = A bolter pierces armor and explodes on impact. One round is damage, a micro-blast, and a slowdown all at once.
wh40k-tips-dataset-57 = The Londoron sniper rifle one-shots, but needs aiming. Prone, aim, fire, reposition — repeat.
wh40k-tips-dataset-58 = The heavy bolter is a stationary turret: deploy, anchor, and the operator swings the barrel. No anchor, no shooting.
wh40k-tips-dataset-59 = The autocannon punches armor and explodes. Save it for armored targets and enemy clusters.
wh40k-tips-dataset-60 = The Mechanicus rad-carbine irradiates the target: damage plus radiation. Don't stand next to the target after a volley — the radiation is area-based.
wh40k-tips-dataset-61 = The Tau Pulse carbine hits harder up close, weaker at range. Close the distance — long range isn't your thing.
wh40k-tips-dataset-62 = NoizeMarine sonic weapons slice flesh with sound and slow it. The Blastmaster is mini-artillery with a shockwave.
wh40k-tips-dataset-63 = The flamethrower floods fire and ignites. Ideal for clearing trenches and barricades — but watch the fuel tank.
wh40k-tips-dataset-64 = Frag grenade for crowds, Krak for armor, Melta for vehicles. Don't mix them up: fragmentation won't crack armor, and anti-tank won't splash a crowd.
wh40k-tips-dataset-65 = The Flak vest takes one plate: laser, bullet, or melee. Pick the one that matches the threat on your front.
wh40k-tips-dataset-66 = Armor plates wear out from hits. Check them between fights and swap the broken ones.
wh40k-tips-dataset-67 = The Voidsman hardsuit blocks radiation, acid, and vacuum. Wear it when storming contaminated zones.
wh40k-tips-dataset-68 = Astartes armor reflects some projectiles and holds pressure. A Space Marine in plate is a walking fortress.
wh40k-tips-dataset-69 = Ork "Ard" armor is tough but heavy — it slows you badly. Wear it only if you plan to tank.
wh40k-tips-dataset-70 = The mortar fires at coordinates. Pre-register with a rangefinder or flare, or the shell goes nowhere.
wh40k-tips-dataset-71 = The rangefinder marks a target for the mortar. Hold the aim while you fire — let go and the marker vanishes.
wh40k-tips-dataset-72 = A signal flare is a backup target designator for the mortar. Fire it over the enemy position and the gunner sees the strike point.
wh40k-tips-dataset-73 = An incendiary mortar shell sets the ground and foliage alight. Don't drop it on your own lines — fire doesn't check uniforms.
wh40k-tips-dataset-74 = The intel detector finds your faction's mission objectives in a radius. Switch range to suit the task: short scans more often, long reaches farther.
wh40k-tips-dataset-75 = The mission pinpointer leads to the active mission target. If the target's gone, it switches to the global one — watch the arrow.
wh40k-tips-dataset-76 = The faction cargo account is shared by the whole team. Don't blow the balance on trinkets — save up for heavy weapons and plasma.
wh40k-tips-dataset-77 = The field chirurgeon can pull a skull from a corpse and turn it into a servo-skull. Don't waste bodies — they become useful tech.
wh40k-tips-dataset-78 = CPR can bring a critical ally back with a small chance. Don't abandon the downed — try to revive them.
wh40k-tips-dataset-79 = You can't heal an enemy with a defib or syringe — the system blocks aid to opponents. Focus on your own.
wh40k-tips-dataset-80 = The conveyor manipulator auto-drags items from one tile to another. Set up production lines without manual hauling.
wh40k-tips-dataset-81 = A squad disbands when its leader dies. Don't throw an officer under fire — five fighters stand behind them and would be left without a commander.
wh40k-tips-dataset-82 = Influence is passive income for the team. Capture three points and hold them, and the treasury fills itself.
wh40k-tips-dataset-83 = In preparation, influence points can't be captured. Use the time to take positions nearby — you'll grab them first in the assault.
wh40k-tips-dataset-84 = A contested point (even forces) freezes progress. Pull up one more fighter to tip the balance.
wh40k-tips-dataset-85 = Faction colors: gold for Imperium, dark red for Heretics. On the tactical map you see at a glance whose point is whose.
wh40k-tips-dataset-86 = The Mechanicus is the Imperium's technical wing. The Magos and crew drive research and build machines.
wh40k-tips-dataset-87 = The Dark Mechanicum is the heretek branch. Their gifts and tech feed on Chaos as much as their weapons do.
wh40k-tips-dataset-88 = Chaos Astartes are the same superhumans, but with gifts from Khorne, Nurgle, Slaanesh, or Tzeentch. No weaker than the loyalists, often stronger.
wh40k-tips-dataset-89 = The Tau are a separate faction with their own roles: Shas'la, Shas'ui, Ethereal. They don't join Team Battle, but appear in free spawn.
wh40k-tips-dataset-90 = Ork Boyz are the simplest role: grab and fight. Perfect for newcomers to get the hang of combat.
wh40k-tips-dataset-91 = Meta-progress accrues between rounds. Levels, achievements, and skill points stay on your account forever.
wh40k-tips-dataset-92 = Character development branches are organ boosts: brain, lungs, kidneys, heart, liver, stomach. Spend skill points thoughtfully.
wh40k-tips-dataset-93 = Decorations are OOC titles, name colors, and ghost skins. Some unlock only via achievements or through Discord.
wh40k-tips-dataset-94 = The "No One Left Behind" achievement is earned by stabilizing allies. A medic grinds progress too — killing isn't the only way.
wh40k-tips-dataset-95 = Veteran of Wars is an achievement for finishing many rounds. Just play regularly and the experience flows on its own.
wh40k-tips-dataset-96 = Victory Parade is the achievement for wins. Play the faction that wins more, or carry yours to victory.
wh40k-tips-dataset-97 = In Prop Hunt the hider can morph into an object. Pick immobile props — chairs, plants, crates — and don't move.
wh40k-tips-dataset-98 = In Prop Hunt the seeker is frozen at the start. Use that time as a hider to grab the best spots and disguise.
wh40k-tips-dataset-99 = In Murder Mystery the murderer can throw smoke and blind everyone. Use it to vanish after a strike or sneak up unseen.
wh40k-tips-dataset-100 = In Gun Game the combat knife is always in your other hand. If the ammo's out — slash until the next weapon comes.
